S2-v3 (.443 A1, exp4811) re-ran the engine-selection test corpus-wide: n_available=25,
n_attempted=25, n_effective=23 (vs S2-v2's 5/25), positive_control_passed, DEGENERATE_
CANDIDATE_POOL does not fire. Verdict complete_structural_energy_s2v3_bounded_corpus_wide,
delta +0.091, CI [-0.063, +0.264] (includes 0). The point estimate FLIPPED from -0.158
(n=5) to +0.091 (n=23) -- the 5-game S2-v2 had the wrong sign; the operator's narrowness
concern was right. Robust read: at engine SELECTION the energy is roughly NEUTRAL (slightly
positive, not significant). Selection is settled corpus-wide. Per the gate, BOUNDED -> S3
(generation lift, the ARC wall, a different mechanism). The 23/25 effective also refutes the
'only a few games form diverse pools' hypothesis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
